d2a|n|In the form of, or bounded by, a circle; round. ; repeating itself; ending in itself; reverting to the point of beginning; hence, illogical; inconclusive; as, circular reasoning. ; Adhering to a fixed circle of legends; cyclic; hence, mean; inferior. See Cyclic poets, under Cyclic. ; Addressed to a circle, or to a number of persons having a common interest; circulated, or intended for circulation; as, a circular letter. ; Perfect; complete. ; A circular letter, or paper, usually printed, copies of which are addressed or given to various persons; as, a business circular. ; A sleeveless cloak, cut in circular form.	N:yzf,49,2~yzf,49,2
d2a|a|In the form of, or bounded by, a circle; round. ; repeating itself; ending in itself; reverting to the point of beginning; hence, illogical; inconclusive; as, circular reasoning. ; Adhering to a fixed circle of legends; cyclic; hence, mean; inferior. See Cyclic poets, under Cyclic. ; Addressed to a circle, or to a number of persons having a common interest; circulated, or intended for circulation; as, a circular letter. ; Perfect; complete. ; A circular letter, or paper, usually printed, copies of which are addressed or given to various persons; as, a business circular. ; A sleeveless cloak, cut in circular form.	j:h89,81,6;1vrh,76,3;1c7n,70,5;1ekq,62,5;209h,60,4;yzf,54,3;1vra,54,3;1i73,51,2~h89,81,6;1c7n,70,5;1ekq,62,5;209h,60,4;1vra,54,3;yzf,54,3;1vrh,76,3;1i73,51,2	e:1iwk,51,3~1iwk,51,3
