d2g|n|The act of moving in a circle, or in a course which brings the moving body to the place where its motion began. ; The act of passing from place to place or person to person; free diffusion; transmission. ; Currency; circulating coin; notes, bills, etc., current for coin. ; The extent to which anything circulates or is circulated; the measure of diffusion; as, the circulation of a newspaper. ; The movement of the blood in the blood-vascular system, by which it is brought into close relations with almost every living elementary constituent. Also, the movement of the sap in the vessels and tissues of plants.	n:1vb,92,7~1vb,92,7	N:rnc,71,3~rnc,71,3
d54|n|That which attends, or relates to, or in some way affects, a fact or event; an attendant thing or state of things. ; An event; a fact; a particular incident. ; Circumlocution; detail. ; Condition in regard to worldly estate; state of property; situation; surroundings.	a:r7y,116,1~r7y,116,1	v:r7y,116,1~r7y,116,1
