d7n|n|One who enjoys the freedom and privileges of a city; a freeman of a city, as distinguished from a foreigner, or one not entitled to its franchises. ; An inhabitant of a city; a townsman. ; A person, native or naturalized, of either sex, who owes allegiance to a government, and is entitled to reciprocal protection from it. ; One who is domiciled in a country, and who is a citizen, though neither native nor naturalized, in such a sense that he takes his legal status from such country.	a:11w6,109,3~11w6,109,3	N:1u7w,40,1~1u7w,40,1
d7n|a|Having the condition or qualities of a citizen, or of citizens; as, a citizen soldiery. ; Of or pertaining to the inhabitants of a city; characteristic of citizens; effeminate; luxurious.	j:1u7w,63,5~1u7w,63,5
